s learned line takes form \\(y = mx + b\\) \\(m\\) slope \\(b\\) y-intercept. Statisticians write equation slightly different form:\\[\n\\hat{y} = b_{0} + b_{1} x\n\\]intercept \\(b_{0}\\) slope \\(b_{1}\\). use \\(\\hat{y}\\) (pronounced “y hat”) instead \\(y\\) plug values \\(x\\), get back exact values \\(y\\) data. line, , actually pass () actual data points. Instead, equation gives us “predicted” values \\(y\\) lie regression line. predicted \\(y\\) values called \\(\\hat{y}\\).run regression analysis calculate values intercept slope, use lm command R. (, lm stands “linear model”.) command requires us specify “formula” tells R relationship want model. uses special syntax specific order:response variable,“tilde” ~ (key usually upper-left corner keyboard, backtick),predictor variable.comma, specify data set variables live using data =. ’s whole command:response variable always goes tilde predictor variable always goes .Let’s store result future use. convention ’ll use book name things using variables involved. example,variable involact_race_lm now contains information need linear regression model.","code":"\nlm(involact ~ race, data = chredlin)## \n## Call:\n## lm(formula = involact ~ race, data = chredlin)\n## \n## Coefficients:\n## (Intercept)         race  \n##     0.12922      0.01388\ninvolact_race_lm <- lm(involact ~ race, data = chredlin)\ninvolact_race_lm## \n## Call:\n## lm(formula = involact ~ race, data = chredlin)\n## \n## Coefficients:\n## (Intercept)         race  \n##     0.12922      0.01388"},{"path":"regression.html","id":"regression-interpreting","chapter":"7 Regression","heading":"7.6 Interpreting the coefficients","text":"Look output lm command .intercept 0.12922 slope 0.01388. number 0.12922 labeled (Intercept), ’s pretty obvious. know number 0.01388 corresponds slope? Process elimination, suppose. ’s another good reason . equation regression line can written\\[\n\\hat{y} = 0.12922 + 0.01388 x\n\\]report equation regression line, typically use words instead \\(\\hat{y}\\) \\(x\\) make equation interpretable context problem. example, data, write equation \\[\n\\widehat{involact} = 0.12922 + 0.01388 race\n\\]slope coefficient race, number attached race. (intercept attached anything; ’s just constant term front .)slope \\(b_{1}\\) always interpretable. model predicts one unit increase x-direction corresponds change 0.01388 units y-direction. Let’s phrase way:model predicts increase one percentage point composition racial minorities corresponds increase 0.01388 new FAIR policies per 100 housing units.intercept \\(b_{0}\\) different story. always literal interpretation:model predicts ZIP code 0% racial minorites generate 0.12922 new FAIR policies.cases (rarely), interpretation might make sense. cases, though, physically impossible predictor variable take value 0, value 0 way outside range data. Whenever use model make prediction outside reasonable values, call extrapolation.Chicago data, likely don’t case extrapolation. literally true ZIP code 0% racial minorities, can see scatterplot values close zero.","code":""},{"path":"regression.html","id":"exercise-4-3","chapter":"7 Regression","heading":"Exercise 4","text":"Use arrange command dplyr sort chredlin data frame race (using default ascending order). value race three ZIP codes smallest percentage minority residents?Please write answer ., even though ZIP codes 0% racial minorities, bunch close zero, literal interpretation intercept also likely sensible one case.","code":"\n# Add code here to sort by race"},{"path":"regression.html","id":"exercise-5-3","chapter":"7 Regression","heading":"Exercise 5","text":"Let’s think something else intercept might telling us case. presumption FAIR policies obtained mostly folks can’t get insurance policies ways. driven racial discrimination, maybe . intercept say number FAIR policies obtained due denial coverage racial discrimination?Please write answer .","code":""},{"path":"regression.html","id":"regression-rescaling","