e.)can grab estimate column dollar sign ’ve seen :“vector” two values, intercept slope, respectively.want one value time? can grab individual elements vector using square brackets follows:interpretation slope , time, ’ll use inline code:model predicts increase 1 percentage points composition racial minorities corresponds increase 0.0138824 new FAIR policies per 100 housing units.Click somewhere inside backticks line hit Ctrl-Enter Cmd-Enter (PC Mac respectively). see number 0.01388235 pop . Preview HTML version document, also see number (code).want apply re-scaling make number interpretable? stuff inside inline code chunk just R code, can kind calculation want.model predicts increase 10 percentage points composition racial minorities corresponds increase 0.1388235 new FAIR policies per 100 housing units.Now number 0.1388235, ten times large.","code":"\ninvolact_race_lm## \n## Call:\n## lm(formula = involact ~ race, data = chredlin)\n## \n## Coefficients:\n## (Intercept)         race  \n##     0.12922      0.01388\ntidy(involact_race_lm)\ninvolact_race_tidy <- tidy(involact_race_lm)\ninvolact_race_tidy\ninvolact_race_tidy$estimate## [1] 0.12921803 0.01388235\ninvolact_race_tidy$estimate[1]## [1] 0.129218\ninvolact_race_tidy$estimate[2]## [1] 0.01388235"},{"path":"regression.html","id":"exercise-7-1","chapter":"7 Regression","heading":"Exercise 7","text":"Copy paste interpretation intercept earlier, replace number 0.12922 inline code chunk grabs number estimate column involact_race_tidy tibble. (Remember intercept first element vector, second element like slope.)Please write answer .","code":""},{"path":"regression.html","id":"regression-residuals","chapter":"7 Regression","heading":"7.9 Residuals","text":"Earlier, promised revisit topic residuals. Residuals measured vertical distances data point regression line. can see visually . (Don’t worry complexity ggplot code used create picture. need create plot like , just focus graph created .)graph shows regression line two residuals red line segments. (residual 47 ZIP codes; two shown graph.) one left corresponds ZIP code 35% racial minority. regression line predicts , model true, ZIP code value involact 0.6. actual data ZIP code involact value 1. residual difference, 0.4. words, true data point 0.4 units higher model prediction. represents positive residual; actual data 0.4 units line. Data points lie regression line negative residuals.","code":"\nggplot(chredlin, aes(y = involact, x = race)) +\n    geom_segment(x = 35.1, xend  = 35.1,\n                 y = 0.6164886, yend = 0.6164886 + 0.38351139,\n                 color = \"red\", size = 2) +\n    geom_segment(x = 66.1, xend = 66.1,\n                 y = 1.0468415, yend = 1.0468415 - 0.64684154,\n                 color = \"red\", size = 2) +\n    geom_point() +\n    geom_smooth(method = lm, se = FALSE)## Warning: Using `size` aesthetic for lines was deprecated in ggplot2 3.4.0.\n## ℹ Please use `linewidth` instead.\n## This warning is displayed once every 8 hours.\n## Call `lifecycle::last_lifecycle_warnings()` to see where this warning was\n## generated.## `geom_smooth()` using formula = 'y ~ x'"},{"path":"regression.html","id":"exercise-8-2","chapter":"7 Regression","heading":"Exercise 8","text":"Look residual right. corresponds ZIP code 66% racial minorities. First, estimate value involact model predicts ZIP code. (y-value point regression line.) Next, report actual involact value ZIP code. Finally, subtract two numbers get approximate value residual. residual positive number negative number?can just estimate eyeballs now. don’t need super precise.Please write answer .formally, let’s call residual \\(e\\). standard notation, “e” stands “error”. , though, ’s error sense mistake. ’s error sense model perfectly accurate, doesn’t predict data points exactly. degree prediction misses “error” “residual”. given following formula:\\[\ne = y - \\hat{y}\n\\]","code":""},{"path":"regression.html","id":"exercise-9-1","chapter":"7 Regressi