ency table, need computations using proportions. (Remember use percentages communicate human beings, math proportions.) Fortunately, output tabyl tibble! can manipulate grab elements need.Let’s create store tabyl output proportions. don’t need marginal distribution, can dispense adorn_totals.","code":"\n# Add code here to create a contingency table of percentages\ndecision_sex_tabyl <- tabyl(sex_discrimination, decision, sex) %>%\n    adorn_percentages(\"col\")\ndecision_sex_tabyl"},{"path":"randomization2.html","id":"exercise-5-5","chapter":"9 Introduction to randomization, Part 2","heading":"Exercise 5","text":"Interpret proportions context data. words, proportions say male files recommended promotion versus female files recommended promotion?Please write answer .real statistic interest us difference proportions. can use mutate command dplyr variable compute difference us.matter fact, know difference promotion rates, don’t really need individual proportions anymore. transmute verb version mutate gives us exactly want. create new column just like mutate, keeps new column. ’ll call resulting output decision_sex_diff.Notice order subtraction: ’re men’s rates minus women’s rates.computes difference promotion rates (first row) difference -promoted rates (second row). Let’s just keep first row, since care promotion rates. (’s success category.) can use slice grab first row:means 29% difference male files promoted female files promoted. difference computed males minus females, fact number positive means male files likely recommended promotion.","code":"\ndecision_sex_tabyl %>%\n    mutate(diff = male - female)\ndecision_sex_diff <- decision_sex_tabyl %>%\n    transmute(diff = male - female)\ndecision_sex_diff\ndecision_sex_diff %>%\n    slice(1)"},{"path":"randomization2.html","id":"randomization2-permuting","chapter":"9 Introduction to randomization, Part 2","heading":"9.5 Permuting","text":"One way see evidence association promotion decisions sex assume, temporarily, association. truly association, difference promotion rates male files female files 0%. course, number people promoted data 35, odd number, number male files promoted female files promoted . Therefore, difference proportions can’t exactly 0 data. Nevertheless, expect—assumption association—number male files promoted close number female files promoted, giving difference around 0%.Now, saw difference 29% two groups data. , non-zero differences—sometimes even large ones— can just come pure chance alone. may accidentally sampled bank managers just happened prefer male candidates. happen sexist reasons; ’s possible sample bank managers , chance, sexist bank managers general population 1970s. might benign reasons; perhaps male applications got randomly steered bank managers likely impressed application, therefore, likely promote anyone regardless gender listed. consider possibility observed difference seems large even though may association promotion sex general population.test range values arise just chance alone? words, explore sampling variability?One way force variables independent “permute”—words, shuffle—values sex data. ignore sex listed file give random label (independent actual sex listed file), know sure assignment random due actual evidence sexism. case, promotion equally likely occur groups.Let’s see permuting works R. begin , look actual values sex data:males happen listed first, followed females.Now permute values around (using sample command). explained earlier chapter, set seed results reproducible.without seed, just make sure ’s truly random:","code":"\nsex_discrimination$sex##  [1] male   male   male   male   male   male   male   male   male   male  \n## [11] male   male   male   male   male   male   male   male   male   male  \n## [21] male   male   male   male   female female female female female female\n## [31] female female female female female female female female female female\n## [41] female female female female female female female female\n## Level