sb2 smoking data set.","code":"\nlibrary(tidyverse)## ── Attaching core tidyverse packages ──────────────────────── tidyverse 2.0.0 ──\n## ✔ dplyr     1.1.2     ✔ readr     2.1.4\n## ✔ forcats   1.0.0     ✔ stringr   1.5.0\n## ✔ ggplot2   3.4.2     ✔ tibble    3.2.1\n## ✔ lubridate 1.9.2     ✔ tidyr     1.3.0\n## ✔ purrr     1.0.2     \n## ── Conflicts ────────────────────────────────────────── tidyverse_conflicts() ──\n## ✖ dplyr::filter() masks stats::filter()\n## ✖ dplyr::lag()    masks stats::lag()\n## ℹ Use the conflicted package (<http://conflicted.r-lib.org/>) to force all conflicts to become errors\nlibrary(janitor)## \n## Attaching package: 'janitor'\n## \n## The following objects are masked from 'package:stats':\n## \n##     chisq.test, fisher.test\nlibrary(infer)\nlibrary(openintro)## Loading required package: airports\n## Loading required package: cherryblossom\n## Loading required package: usdata"},{"path":"ci.html","id":"ci-boot","chapter":"12 Confidence intervals","heading":"12.3 Bootstrapping","text":"Imagine obtain random sample 200 high school seniors across U.S. Suppose 32 attend private school. sample statistic, \\[\n\\hat{p} = 32/200 = 0.16\n\\]\nwords, 16% students sample attended private school.sample representative, might guess true population parameter \\(p\\) also close 0.16, ’re really sure:\\[\np \\approx 0.16?\n\\]sampling variability? chapters ago, flipped coins. “weighted” coin flipped 200 times can give us “new” (fake) sample, thousand times (even ) can give us lot new samples see range values possible. use probability heads weighted coin? bad idea use 0.16 assume population proportion agreed exactly one sample happen . worked hypothesis test value \\(p\\) assumed true guise null hypothesis. general, simply want estimate population parameter sample statistic, information use. coin flipping .alternative available us procedure called bootstrapping. idea sounds weird, ’s pretty simple: instead building fake samples, tried build fake popu