relatively wide range values seem possible outcomes surveys. Nevertheless, range values mostly 50%. Nevertheless, small chance survey give us “wrong” answer predict defeat candidate.19","code":"\nset.seed(13579)\nsurvey_sim <- do(1000) * rflip(50, prob = 0.64)\nggplot(survey_sim, aes(x = prop)) +\n    geom_histogram(binwidth = 0.01) +\n    geom_vline(xintercept = 0.5, color = \"blue\")\npdist(\"norm\", q = 0.5,\n      mean = 0.64, sd = sqrt(0.64 * (1 - 0.64) / 50))## [1] 0.01958508"},{"path":"samp-dist-models.html","id":"exercise-7a-3","chapter":"14 Sampling distribution models","heading":"Exercise 7(a)","text":"Suppose testing new drug intended reduce cholesterol levels patients high cholesterol. Also suppose drug works 83% patients. testing drug, use suitably random sample 143 individuals high cholesterol.First, simulate sampling distribution using 1000 samples, size 143. Plot resulting sampling distribution.","code":"\nset.seed(13579)\n# Add code here to simulate 1000 samples of size 143\n# and plot the resulting distribution."},{"path":"samp-dist-models.html","id":"exercise-7b-3","chapter":"14 Sampling distribution models","heading":"Exercise 7(b)","text":"Next, check conditions allow use normal model sampling distribution model. ’ve given outline :Random\n[Check condition .]\n[Check condition .]10%\n[Check condition .]\n[Check condition .]Success/failure\n[Check condition .]\n[Check condition .]","code":""},{"path":"samp-dist-models.html","id":"exercise-7c-2","chapter":"14 Sampling distribution models","heading":"Exercise 7(c)","text":"conditions met, can use normal model sampling distribution model. mean standard error model? (use inline R code calculate report standard error.)Please write answer .","code":""},{"path":"samp-dist-models.html","id":"exercise-7d","chapter":"14 Sampling distribution models","heading":"Exercise 7(d)","text":"Market analysis shows unless drug effective 85% patients, doctors won’t prescribe . Secretly, know true rate effectiveness 83%, manufacturer doesn’t know yet. access drug trial data 143 patients high cholesterol.Using normal model just developed, determine likely drug trial data show drug “effective” according 85% standard. words, often sample give us result 85% higher (even though secretly know true effectiveness 83%)? Report answer contextually-meaningful full sentence using inline R code. (Hint: ’ll need use pdist command.)Please write answer .","code":""},{"path":"samp-dist-models.html","id":"samp-dist-models-conclusion","chapter":"14 Sampling distribution models","heading":"14.7 Conclusion","text":"easy work normal models. Therefore, want study sampling variability, useful normal model sampling distribution model. standard error measure variable random samples can . variability naturally decreases sample size grows. (makes sense: larger samples give us precise estimates true population, “closer” true population value.) conditions checked, can use normal models make predictions likely see sample population.","code":""},{"path":"samp-dist-models.html","id":"samp-dist-models-prep","chapter":"14 Sampling distribution models","heading":"14.7.1 Preparing and submitting your assignment","text":"“Run” menu, select “Restart R Run Chunks”.Deal code errors crop . Repeat steps 1–-2 code errors.Spell check document clicking icon “ABC” check mark.Hit “Preview” button one last time generate final draft .nb.html file.Proofread HTML file carefully. errors, go back fix , repeat steps 1–5 .completed chapter part statistics course, follow directions receive professor submit assignment.","code":""},{"path":"one-prop.html","id":"one-prop","chapter":"15 Inference for one proportion","heading":"15 Inference for one proportion","text":"\n2.0\n","code":""},{"path":"one-prop.html","id":"functions-introduced-in-this-chapter-14","chapter":"15 Inference for one proportion","heading":"Functions introduced in this chapter","text":"new R functions introduced .","code":""},{"path":"one-prop.html","id":"one-prop-intro