io make sure ’re intro_stats project. click following link download chapter R notebook file (.Rmd).https://vectorposse.github.io/intro_stats/chapter_downloads/20-inference_for_paired_data.RmdOnce file downloaded, move project folder RStudio open .","code":""},{"path":"inference-for-paired-data.html","id":"restart-r-and-run-all-chunks-4","chapter":"20 Inference for paired data","heading":"20.1.3 Restart R and run all chunks","text":"RStudio, select “Restart R Run Chunks” “Run” menu.","code":""},{"path":"inference-for-paired-data.html","id":"load-packages-4","chapter":"20 Inference for paired data","heading":"20.2 Load packages","text":"load standard tidyverse infer packages. openintro package give access textbooks data hsb2 data.","code":"\nlibrary(tidyverse)## ── Attaching core tidyverse packages ──────────────────────── tidyverse 2.0.0 ──\n## ✔ dplyr     1.1.2     ✔ readr     2.1.4\n## ✔ forcats   1.0.0     ✔ stringr   1.5.0\n## ✔ ggplot2   3.4.2     ✔ tibble    3.2.1\n## ✔ lubridate 1.9.2     ✔ tidyr     1.3.0\n## ✔ purrr     1.0.2     \n## ── Conflicts ────────────────────────────────────────── tidyverse_conflicts() ──\n## ✖ dplyr::filter() masks stats::filter()\n## ✖ dplyr::lag()    masks stats::lag()\n## ℹ Use the conflicted package (<http://conflicted.r-lib.org/>) to force all conflicts to become errors\nlibrary(infer)\nlibrary(openintro)## Loading required package: airports\n## Loading required package: cherryblossom\n## Loading required package: usdata"},{"path":"inference-for-paired-data.html","id":"paired-data","chapter":"20 Inference for paired data","heading":"20.3 Paired data","text":"Sometimes data sets two numerical variables related . example, diet study might include pre-weight post-weight. research question either variables directly, rather difference variables, example much weight lost diet.case, run inference paired data. procedure involves calculating new variable d represents difference two paired variables. null hypothesis almost always difference paired variables, translates statement average value d zero.","code":""},{"path":"inference-for-paired-data.html","id":"research-question-4","chapter":"20 Inference for paired data","heading":"20.4 Research question","text":"textbooks data frame (openintro package) data price books UCLA bookstore versus Amazon.com. question interest whether campus bookstore charges Amazon.","code":""},{"path":"inference-for-paired-data.html","id":"inference-for-paired-data-1","chapter":"20 Inference for paired data","heading":"20.5 Inference for paired data","text":"key idea don’t actually care book prices . care difference prices book. two independent variables row represents single book. Therefore, two measurements “paired” treated single numerical variable interest, representing difference ucla_new amaz_new.Since ’re interested analyzing one numerical variable d, process nothing one-sample t test. Therefore, really nothing new chapter.Let’s go rubric.","code":""},{"path":"inference-for-paired-data.html","id":"exploratory-data-analysis-11","chapter":"20 Inference for paired data","heading":"20.6 Exploratory data analysis","text":"","code":""},{"path":"inference-for-paired-data.html","id":"use-data-documentation-help-files-code-books-google-etc.-to-determine-as-much-as-possible-about-the-data-provenance-and-structure.-11","chapter":"20 Inference for paired data","heading":"20.6.1 Use data documentation (help files, code books, Google, etc.) to determine as much as possible about the data provenance and structure.","text":"type textbooks Console read help file. data collected person, David Diez. quick Google search reveals statistician graduated UCLA. presume access accurate information prices books UCLA bookstore Amazon.com time data collected.data set:two paired variables ucla_new amaz_new.","code":"\ntextbooks\nglimpse(textbooks)## Rows: 73\n## Columns: 7\n## $ dept_abbr <fct> Am Ind, Anthro, Anthro, Anthro, Art His, Art His, Asia Am, A…\n## $ course    <fct>  C170, 9, 135T,